               in computer algebra systems. Designed to accompany one- or
               two-semester courses for advanced undergraduate or graduate
               students in computer science or mathematics, its
               comprehensiveness and reliability has also made it an essential
               reference for professionals in the area. Special features
               include: detailed study of algorithms including time analysis;
               implementation reports on several topics; complete proofs of the
               mathematical underpinnings; and a wide variety of applications
               (among others, in chemistry, coding theory, cryptography,
